WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.801
-And you know what?

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.103
Those jokes were
mostly pretty good.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.337
But to get those 10 or 11 jokes,

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.805
our monologue writers
have to write

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.640
hundreds of jokes every day.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.310
And I'll be honest with you,
they're not all good.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.245
And, honestly, sometimes,
I think they throw in

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.314
some real stinkers
just to fill up a page

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.184
and meet the assignment,
which is understandable.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.319
Joke writing is a grind,
and they work really hard.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.588
But now that we
have audiences again,

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:23.623
that kind of laziness --

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.791
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:28.060
Yeah, give yourselves
a round of applause.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.729
That kind of laziness
has got to stop,

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.232
which means it's time for a
"Surprise Inspection."

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:38.738
[ Fanfare ]

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.173
Way too long.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.208
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.481
So, here's how this works.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:52.251
These jokes -- These are real
jokes submitted by my writers

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:53.987
that are unusable for the show.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.923
Some are dumb,
some are patently offensive,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.859
and some are just baffling.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.928
Most importantly, the writers
don't know we're doing this,

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.063
and because a lot of them
don't watch the show,

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:06.832
they'll never know
that we're doing this.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.901
So, let's get to it.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.438
A Eurasian eagle owl named
Gladys recently escaped from

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:15.141
a zoo in Minnesota after
she flew into a tree

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.810
during a training session
and did not return.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.412
Her friends were no help.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.946
When asked if
they had seen Gladys,

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:22.982
all they said was, "Who?"

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.851
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:27.887
Don't.
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:35.127
Brian wrote that joke.
There's a picture of Brian.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:36.596
Brian is a dad,

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:41.501
so it's okay for him to tell
a stupid [bleep] dad joke.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.404
It's legal.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:49.242
Michigan State University
recently asked faculty and staff

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.977
to volunteer to work in the
dining halls without extra pay

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:53.879
amid an ongoing labor shortage.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.950
Luckily, the Jell-O has tenure.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.219
I fully don't get it.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.689
Makes no sense to me.
Baze, does it make sense to you?

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.558
-No.
-Okay, good.

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.729
It was just like,
"Jell-O's funny."

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.599
Matt Goldich wrote that.
Let's see Matt. There he is.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.104
Matt made of Jell-O.

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:23.242
Amid global supply-chain delays,
toy makers, reportedly,

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.578
are planning to release more
small, squishy toys

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.846
this holiday season.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.615
"You mean rabbits?",
asked Lennie?

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:38.557
So, that joke requires
a very specific knowledge of

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:43.395
the book or film
"Of Mice and Men,"

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:46.932
where Lennie does not know
his strength.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.002
He kills rabbits.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.704
Squishes them so hard
that he kills them.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.640
'Cause some people don't know
their own strength,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.808
so then they harm people.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:03:00.012
Other people don't know
their own weakness

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:04.750
and they wear tank tops to work,
like Scollins...

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.352
who wrote that joke.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:10.623
According a new survey,
half of Americans said

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.358
if they could time-travel,
they would prefer

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.893
to move forward in time.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.596
"Thank you," said baby Hitler.

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.669
And, again, you might not
think that joke is funny,

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:25.704
but here is
something that's very funny.

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:29.275
Someone allowed their child to
be used for stock photos.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:35.582
"What's the worst they can do?"

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.786
According to new reports,
some areas of the country

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:42.188
are experiencing
a pumpkin shortage,

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.356
but in other news,

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:46.158
there has been a surplus of
jack-o'-lanterns.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:47.794
Oof.

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:53.766
I almost feel bad showing you --
Like, you literally --

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.234
Not one of you went for a joke

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.635
by the nicest person
on our staff.

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:58.805
That's Karen.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.506
Too late.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.779
According to new reports,
some areas of the country

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.381
are experiencing
a pumpkin shortage,

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.316
which will cause prices
to increase.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:14.487
It's a phenomenon known to
economists as "pumpkinflation."

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:18.858
Ian.

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:21.193
According to new reports,

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:23.796
a drought in California
has caused a pumpkin shortage.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.465
This is one of the nice things
about working at this show,

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:29.302
is, you know, 'cause they all
hear about pumpkin shortages,

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.403
and then they just grind out

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:35.274
unusable joke
after unusable joke.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:38.077
Let's see -- I'm gonna just say
in advance, it's Ally's joke.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.445
We're 0 for 2 on
pumpkin shortage.

00:04:40.445 --> 00:04:43.582
Karen ate it hard.
Ian ate it hard.

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:46.052
It's up to Ally to save us
on the pumpkin shortage.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.453
Let's see if she can do it.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.021
According to reports,
a drought in California

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.356
has caused a pumpkin shortage.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.259
All we can do now is pray to
gourd for some rain.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.295
[ Light applause, laughter ]

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.636
I think we can say -- I think
the best we could say is

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.406
Ally is the king
of [bleep] mountain.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.513
The indie band Bon Iver
announced yesterday they'll

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.414
launch a U.S.-and-European tour
next year.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.516
But if you want to see them
live, you must have taken

00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:22.021
at least your first dose of
Bon Ivermectin.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.926
Let's take a look at
who has tenure.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.961
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:34.634
A turtle recently hatched
in Massachusetts

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.335
with two heads and six legs,

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:37.970
which,
by Massachusetts standards,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.173
still makes her a 9.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.442
[ Light applause ]

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:45.511
Yeah, you can clap.
You can clap.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.113
Mike Scollins wrote that joke,
and he's from Massachusetts

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:50.316
and he tries to get me
in trouble.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.054
According to a new survey,
19% of Americans

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.223
say that they feel older
than their actual age.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.858
"Yeah, that's not going to
help your case,"

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.993
said R. Kelly's lawyer.

00:06:06.064 --> 00:06:07.400
Same dude.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.868
There he is.

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:12.405
Oh, no. No, no, no.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:17.310
One of them writes for us.
I can never remember.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.819
This segment is over now
and I'm going to say it's over,

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.053
and then we're gonna
have to watch

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:31.991
that awful
graphics package again.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.659
So I just apologize.
Just brace yourselves.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.993
Just zone out for the next --
What?

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:38.231
I think -- What is it?
95 seconds?

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.966
This has been
"Surprise Inspection."

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:46.606
[ Fanfare ]

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.579
Did the title card play?

